counterexample_dsp:
The database contains three view events. Author 1 views their own article (ARTICLE_ID 101). Author 3 views their own article (ARTICLE_ID 103). Additionally, Author 2 views an article (ARTICLE_ID 102) where Viewer ID is 3. For Author 1, there is no *other* view event where 1 is the VIEWER_ID. For Author 3, there is another view event (ARTICLE_ID 102) where 3 is the VIEWER_ID. This setup ensures that ID 1 is returned by Q1 but not by Q2 (due to the implicit distinct row requirement for V1 and V2), while ID 3 is returned by both.

Q1 Result: {1, 3}
Q2 Result: {3}

